    <item>
      <title>Lesson Plan</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/lesson-plan/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/lesson-plan/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;lesson-plan&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Lesson Plan&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#lesson-plan&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In the first few weeks of the class we&amp;rsquo;ll assemble a class kit of materials and supplies that are required for all activities. Please bring this kit with you to class each day.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;section class=&#34;lesson-week&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h2 id=&#34;week-1-welcome&#34;&gt;Week 1 — Welcome&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__desc&#34;&gt;This week we&amp;rsquo;re introducing the class and basics about weaving. &lt;em&gt;(Semester starts Thursday — no Tuesday meeting this week.)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__grid&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__col-label&#34;&gt;Tuesday&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__col-label&#34;&gt;Thursday&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;class-block class-block--empty&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;article class=&#34;class-block&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h3 class=&#34;class-block__title&#34;&gt;8/20 — Class Introduction&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__note&#34;&gt;First day of the semester — class meets Thursday only this week.&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__section&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h4&gt;In class&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;    &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Setting Community Norms&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Questions about How Class Will Take Place&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/pdf/PaperLoom.pdf&#34;&gt;Paper Weaving&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Review &lt;a href=&#34;../material-list&#34;&gt;Required Supplies&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/article&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/section&gt;&#xA;&lt;section class=&#34;lesson-week&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h2 id=&#34;week-2-weaving-and-materials-led-design&#34;&gt;Week 2 — Weaving and Materials-Led Design&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__desc&#34;&gt;This week we&amp;rsquo;re starting our first experiments with weaving alongside and introduction to materials-led design methodologies.&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__grid&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__col-label&#34;&gt;Tuesday&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__col-label&#34;&gt;Thursday&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;article class=&#34;class-block&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h3 class=&#34;class-block__title&#34;&gt;8/25 — Design Philosophy&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__section&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h4&gt;Bring&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;    &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Your class kit&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__section&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h4&gt;In class&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;    &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Discussion of Sampling and Materials-Led Design&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Review &lt;a href=&#34;../templates/weeklies-template&#34;&gt;Weeklies Templates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Assemble Class Kit&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;History Of Presentations&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/article&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;article class=&#34;class-block&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h3 class=&#34;class-block__title&#34;&gt;8/27 — Looms and Weaving&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__section&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h4&gt;Bring&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;    &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Your class kit&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;a not-too-precious hard cover book of your choice&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__section class-block__section--due&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h4&gt;Due&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;    &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Annie Albers, On Weaving, &amp;ldquo;The Loom&amp;rdquo;, pp 23-43 and images on pp 83-89&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/article&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/section&gt;&#xA;&lt;section class=&#34;lesson-week&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h2 id=&#34;week-3-finishing-and-connecting&#34;&gt;Week 3 — Finishing and Connecting&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__desc&#34;&gt;we&amp;rsquo;ll finish our book looms and start making connectors to use in soft circuits.&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__grid&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__col-label&#34;&gt;Tuesday&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__col-label&#34;&gt;Thursday&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;article class=&#34;class-block&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h3 class=&#34;class-block__title&#34;&gt;9/1 — Finishing Techniques&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__section&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h4&gt;Bring&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;    &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Your class kit&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__section class-block__section--due&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h4&gt;Due&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;    &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;../weeklies/1-make-a-book-loom&#34;&gt;Weekly 1 — Make a Book Loom&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/article&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;article class=&#34;class-block&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h3 class=&#34;class-block__title&#34;&gt;9/3 — Conductive Yarns, Multi-meters, and Connectors&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__section&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h4&gt;Bring&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;    &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Your class kit&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__section&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h4&gt;In class&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;    &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;How to use a Multimeter&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Understanding Resistance Worksheet&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Start &lt;a href=&#34;../weeklies/2-make-connectors&#34;&gt;Weekly 2 — Make Connectors&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/article&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/section&gt;&#xA;&lt;section class=&#34;lesson-week&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h2 id=&#34;week-4-warping-and-weaving-with-etta-sandry&#34;&gt;Week 4 — Warping and Weaving with Etta Sandry&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__desc&#34;&gt;we&amp;rsquo;ll start warping and weaving on our Cricket looms and exploring different methods for integrating conductive materials.&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__grid&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__col-label&#34;&gt;Tuesday&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__col-label&#34;&gt;Thursday&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;article class=&#34;class-block&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h3 class=&#34;class-block__title&#34;&gt;9/8 — Warping and Weaving Tabby&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__note&#34;&gt;This class will be guest taught by Etta Sandry&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__section&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h4&gt;Bring&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;    &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Your class kit&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;your completed connectors&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;your cricket loom&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__section class-block__section--due&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h4&gt;Due&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;    &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;../weeklies/2-make-connectors&#34;&gt;Weekly 2 — Make Connectors&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__section&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h4&gt;In class&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;    &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Connector Share Out&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;../worksheets/parts-of-the-loom&#34;&gt;Parts of the Loom Quiz&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Start &lt;a href=&#34;../weeklies/3-warp-and-weave&#34;&gt;Weekly 3 — Warp and Weave&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/article&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;article class=&#34;class-block&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h3 class=&#34;class-block__title&#34;&gt;9/10 — Manipulating Tabby&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__note&#34;&gt;This class will be guest taught by Etta Sandry&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__section&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h4&gt;Bring&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;    &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Your class kit&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;your cricket loom&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__section class-block__section--active&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h4&gt;Active&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;    &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;../weeklies/3-warp-and-weave&#34;&gt;Weekly 3 — Warp and Weave&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;class-block__section&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h4&gt;In class&lt;/h4&gt;&#xA;    &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Tapestry Techniques (weft pile, looping, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;li&gt;Leno and Lace Structures&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/article&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/section&gt;&#xA;&lt;section class=&#34;lesson-week&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h2 id=&#34;week-5-tbd&#34;&gt;Week 5 — TBD&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__grid&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__col-label&#34;&gt;Tuesday&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;lesson-week__col-label&#34;&gt;Thursday&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;article class=&#34;class-block class-block--no-class&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h3 class=&#34;class-block__title&#34;&gt;9/15 — &lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p class=&#34;class-block__banner&#34;&gt;No class&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Syllabus</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/syllabus/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/syllabus/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;syllabus&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Syllabus&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#syllabus&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;instructor&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Instructor&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#instructor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Laura Devendorf&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;Assistant Professor, ATLAS Institute &amp;amp; Dept. of Information Science&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;mailto:laura.devendorf@colorado.edu&#34;&gt;laura.devendorf@colorado.edu&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Office Hours&lt;/strong&gt;&#xA;By Appointment, Wednesdays 3:15-4:15 &amp;amp; Thursdays, 11-12&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://calendly.com/lauradevendorf/oh&#34;&gt;Schedule an Office Hour&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;location-and-timing&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Location and Timing&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#location-and-timing&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Fall 2026 // Tuesday, Thursday: 8:55am - 10:45am&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;&#xA;ATLAS 1B31&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;course-schedule&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Course Schedule&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#course-schedule&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You may view a detailed course schedule &lt;a href=&#34;../lesson-plan&#34;&gt;on the Lesson Plan link&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;course-materials&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Course Materials&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#course-materials&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You may view a detailed list of the materials that will be required for you to purchase or available for you to check out on the &lt;a href=&#34;../material-list&#34;&gt;Materials List&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Student Projects</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/student-projects/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/student-projects/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/images/sasha_1.gif&#34; alt=&#34;Project by Sasha Paulovich&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Students in this course created final projects inspired by the artist talks, examples, and projects through the semester. You can view several of them on the &lt;a href=&#34;https://unstable.design/experimental-textiles-student-projects/&#34;&gt;Unstable Design Lab Website&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Material List</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/material-list/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/material-list/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;material-list&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Material List&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#material-list&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;While most equipment required for the class will be provided, we are asking students to purchase a few materials on their own, as they are ones we expect some might already own. After the first half of the class, each student will refine their direction and may need access to more specific equipment and supplies. In that case, we have created a &amp;ldquo;library&amp;rdquo; for you to check out or take materials as they are required. The instructor will introduce which materials are available and how to access the materials library during the semester.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Shared Loom Setups</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/loom_setups/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/loom_setups/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Shared looms for this class will be housed in 1B25. You will have access to this room via your BuffOne card.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;loom-types&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Loom Types&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#loom-types&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;8S-1: An 8-Shaft Table Top Shaft Loom&#xA;8S-2: An 8-Shaft Table Top Shaft Loom&#xA;BabyWolf: An 8-Shaft Floor Loom&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;student-limits&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Student Limits&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#student-limits&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The class looms are warped with enough yarn to support each student making 3.5 yards of cloth total. Technically, we warp assuming each student will weave 4 yards to account for waste when cutting. Please do not go over your 3.5 limit. With 22 students, 3.5 yards each comes to roughly 77 yards of cloth!&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
